<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <span class="eyebrow">FAQ · 5 questions</span>
    <h2>Common questions, answered.</h2>
    <p>
      The objections that come up most. If something is missing, <a
        class="faq-contact-link"
        href="mailto:hello@sur9e.com">contacting us</a
      > is the easiest way to ask.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-list reveal">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary
        >Is this just another AI resume optimizer? <span
          class="chev"
          aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
      >
      <div class="faq-a">
        Resume optimizers run keyword matches on every posting and tell you what
        to bolt onto your CV. Sur9e leads with the job evaluation — does this
        role even deserve an application? For the ones that do, Sur9e will also
        tailor a CV for that specific posting, grounded in real experience and
        the role's actual signals. Score the job first, write to it second.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary
        >Does Sur9e auto-apply for me? <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"
        ></span></summary
      >
      <div class="faq-a">
        Never. By design. Auto-application has a 2% callback rate and 53% of
        hiring managers reject obviously-AI applications. The Sur9e bet is the
        opposite direction: fewer applications, better fit, warmer paths.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary
        >What data does Sur9e need? <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"
        ></span></summary
      >
      <div class="faq-a">
        A CV, a short profile — goals, salary floor, dealbreakers, projects
        worth surfacing. Roughly 10 minutes to set up. Everything stays in the
        account.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary
        >When does it launch? <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"
        ></span></summary
      >
      <div class="faq-a">
        Q4 2026. Joining the waitlist gets the email the day it ships.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary
        >Is it really free? <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"
        ></span></summary
      >
      <div class="faq-a">
        Yes, at launch. The free tier covers job evaluation. Paid tiers come
        later for power users — the free tier stays.
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

